WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.673
A private AI assistant is an end-to-end system, not merely a local model.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:15.875
Infrastructure, interfaces, knowledge, retrieval, logs, backups, integrations, access, and administration determine its actual privacy.

00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:24.077
Start with a narrow purpose, defined audience, permitted data, prohibited actions, and measurable success.

00:00:24.077 --> 00:00:30.692
Choose hardware, model, quantization, runtime, and interface according to that workload.

00:00:30.692 --> 00:00:38.365
Ground private knowledge through controlled ingestion, retrieval evaluation, source citations, versioning, and authorization.

00:00:38.365 --> 00:00:44.979
Design the interface for usability, correction, transparent history, and human escalation.

00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:52.123
Secure accounts, APIs, networks, secrets, downloads, prompts, documents, indexes, logs, and backups.

00:00:52.123 --> 00:00:59.796
Evaluate the complete workflow for quality, hallucination, latency, memory, stability, permission, and recovery.

00:00:59.796 --> 00:01:07.469
Start small, measure real value, and expand only when the assistant reliably helps.

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:15.142
Strong assistants are useful, maintainable, secure, grounded, honest about uncertainty, and appropriately limited.
